IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P2-art-12.l4 -- ARTICLE 12 OF REGULATION (EU) 2016/679: TRANSPARENT INFORMATION, COMMUNICATION AND MODALITIES
-- FOR THE EXERCISE OF THE RIGHTS OF THE DATA SUBJECT (layer 1).
-- Written by P2 (Sonnet 5.5).  Lines 146-158 of eu-gdpr-2016-679-consolidated-20160504.txt (the Chapter III and
-- Section 1 headings at 142-145 and the two heading lines of Article 12 at 146-147 are `inert` headings).
-- Target compiler: main (build 1.6.112).  Answers: MAYBE BOOLEAN; MAYBE `Duty outcome` for a duty with a gate; a
-- DEONTIC for each regulative rule; one NUMBER (Art 12(3), the months allowed).
--
-- WHOSE.  Article 12 is the controller's duty towards the data subject (the data subject's claim): every duty
-- below is "the controller shall ...", and the data subject is the one who may rely on it.  Article 12(8) (the
-- Commission's power to adopt delegated acts) is machinery and is `inert` (2).
--
-- READING A RESULT (NOTES, "Reading a result").  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Regulation gives in its
-- own words; NOTHING means it does not answer on these facts.  Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- THE CLOCK.  A regulative rule below counts its WITHIN in MONTHS (one month, three months): the text counts
-- "one month of receipt".  A decision function takes the two dates and uses `add months`, which keeps the day of the
-- month and clamps at the end of a short month (31 January plus one month is 28 February).
-- ============================================================================

DECLARE `Art 12 action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 12(1) take appropriate measures to provide the information and communications in the form that paragraph 1 requires`
    `Art 12(2) facilitate the exercise of data subject rights under Articles 15 to 22`
    `Art 12(2) refuse to act on the request of the data subject`
    `Art 12(3) provide the data subject with information on action taken on the request`
    `Art 12(3) inform the data subject of the extension, with the reasons for the delay`
    `Art 12(4) inform the data subject of the reasons for not taking action and of the possibilities of a complaint and a judicial remedy`

§ `Article 12(1): the form of the information and communications`

-- src:148 | The controller shall take appropriate measures to provide any information referred to in Articles 13 and 14 and any communication under Articles 15 to 22 and 34 relating to processing to the data subject in a concise, transparent, intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language, in particular for any information addressed specifically to a child.
@ref Art 12(1) first sentence (src:148)
GIVEN `the controller has taken appropriate measures to provide the information and communications to the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information and communications are concise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information and communications are transparent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information and communications are intelligible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information and communications are in an easily accessible form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information and communications use clear and plain language` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is addressed specifically to a child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(1) the controller takes appropriate measures to provide the information and communications in a concise, transparent, intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language` MEANS
    IF `the controller has taken appropriate measures to provide the information and communications to the data subject`
       AND `the information and communications are concise`
       AND `the information and communications are transparent`
       AND `the information and communications are intelligible`
       AND `the information and communications are in an easily accessible form`
       AND `the information and communications use clear and plain language`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "The controller shall take appropriate measures to provide any information referred to in Articles 13 and 14 and any communication under Articles 15 to 22 and 34 relating to processing to the data subject in a concise, transparent, intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language"
    -- "in particular for any information addressed specifically to a child": `the information is addressed specifically to a child` is not read, by the text's own words ("in particular" stresses a case; it does not add a second test).
    -- "appropriate", "concise", "transparent", "intelligible", "easily accessible", "clear and plain": undefined terms; each is a plain fact the caller states.

GIVEN `the controller has taken appropriate measures to provide the information and communications to the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(1) the controller has taken appropriate measures` MEANS
    IF `the controller has taken appropriate measures to provide the information and communications to the data subject`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "The controller shall take appropriate measures"

-- src:148 | The information shall be provided in writing, or by other means, including, where appropriate, by electronic means.
@ref Art 12(1) second sentence (src:148)
GIVEN `the information is provided in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is provided by other means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is provided by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `electronic means are appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(1) the information is provided in writing, or by other means, including, where appropriate, by electronic means` MEANS
    IF `the information is provided in writing` OR `the information is provided by other means` OR `the information is provided by electronic means`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "The information shall be provided in writing, or by other means"
    -- "including, where appropriate, by electronic means": electronic means are one of "other means", so providing by electronic means answers JUST TRUE; `electronic means are appropriate` is not read (a list that includes, not a condition on the other means).

-- src:148 | When requested by the data subject, the information may be provided orally, provided that the identity of the data subject is proven by other means.
@ref Art 12(1) third sentence (src:148)
GIVEN `the data subject has requested that the information be provided orally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the identity of the data subject is proven by other means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(1) the information may be provided orally` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the data subject has requested that the information be provided orally`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "When", periods ruling (b) with the delegated ruling (c) of 2026-11-05; split site (ii), fork F12-1): "When requested by the data subject, the information may be provided orally"
        IF NOT (`the identity of the data subject is proven by other means`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "provided that"; split site (ii), fork F12-1): "provided that the identity of the data subject is proven by other means"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 12 action`
`Art 12(1) the controller must take appropriate measures to provide the information and communications` MEANS
    PARTY controller
    MUST `Art 12(1) take appropriate measures to provide the information and communications in the form that paragraph 1 requires`
    -- no time limit and no consequence is stated: the rule can stand or be fulfilled and never be breached (NOTES, Rules with no breach path)

§ `Article 12(2): facilitating the rights, and the cases of Article 11(2)`

-- src:149 | The controller shall facilitate the exercise of data subject rights under Articles 15 to 22.
@ref Art 12(2) first sentence (src:149)
GIVEN `the controller has facilitated the exercise of the data subject's rights under Articles 15 to 22` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(2) the controller facilitates the exercise of data subject rights under Articles 15 to 22` MEANS
    IF `the controller has facilitated the exercise of the data subject's rights under Articles 15 to 22`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "The controller shall facilitate the exercise of data subject rights under Articles 15 to 22"
    -- "facilitate": an undefined term; a plain fact the caller states.

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 12 action`
`Art 12(2) the controller must facilitate the exercise of data subject rights under Articles 15 to 22` MEANS
    PARTY controller
    MUST `Art 12(2) facilitate the exercise of data subject rights under Articles 15 to 22`
    -- no time limit and no consequence is stated (NOTES, Rules with no breach path)

-- src:149 | In the cases referred to in Article 11(2), the controller shall not refuse to act on the request of the data subject for exercising his or her rights under Articles 15 to 22, unless the controller demonstrates that it is not in a position to identify the data subject.
@ref Art 12(2) second sentence (src:149)
GIVEN `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the controller demonstrates that it is not in a position to identify the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(2) the controller shall not refuse to act on the request of the data subject in the cases referred to in Article 11(2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the cases referred to in Article 11(2)": P1's answer NOTHING means the case is outside Article 11(2) (or not decided), and a scope pointer with no gate word does not say no (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05, fork F12-2)
        IF `the controller demonstrates that it is not in a position to identify the data subject`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "unless"): "unless the controller demonstrates that it is not in a position to identify the data subject"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a flat negative; JUST TRUE here means the bar stands): "the controller shall not refuse to act on the request of the data subject for exercising his or her rights under Articles 15 to 22" (a flat negative)

GIVEN `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the controller demonstrates that it is not in a position to identify the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 12 action`
`Art 12(2) the controller shall not refuse to act on the request in the cases referred to in Article 11(2)` MEANS
    IF `Art 12(2) the controller shall not refuse to act on the request of the data subject in the cases referred to in Article 11(2)` `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` `the controller demonstrates that it is not in a position to identify the data subject` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY controller
         SHANT `Art 12(2) refuse to act on the request of the data subject`
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- a SHANT with no deadline is breached by the act itself; when the bar does not stand (outside Article 11(2), or the controller demonstrates it cannot identify) the rule is FULFILLED

§ `Article 12(3): one month, the extension, the notice, electronic means`

-- The months allowed: "within one month", and "That period may be extended by two further months".
-- src:150 | The controller shall provide information on action taken on a request under Articles 15 to 22 to the data subject without undue delay and in any event within one month of receipt of the request.
@ref Art 12(3) first sentence: the months allowed (src:150)
GIVEN `the period has been extended by two further months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Art 12(3) the months within which the information on action taken is to be provided` MEANS
    IF `the period has been extended by two further months`
    THEN 3
    ELSE 1

-- src:150 | The controller shall inform the data subject of any such extension within one month of receipt of the request, together with the reasons for the delay.
@ref Art 12(3) third sentence: the months allowed for the notice of the extension (src:150)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Art 12(3) the months within which the data subject is to be informed of the extension` MEANS
    1
-- "within one month of receipt of the request": the notice has no extended period (the two further months belong to the information on action taken).

-- src:150 | The controller shall provide information on action taken on a request under Articles 15 to 22 to the data subject without undue delay and in any event within one month of receipt of the request.
@ref Art 12(3) first sentence (src:150)
GIVEN `the date the controller received the request` IS A DATE
      `the date the controller provided the information on action taken` IS A DATE
      `the controller provided the information on action taken without undue delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period has been extended by two further months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(3) the controller provides information on action taken on the request without undue delay and within one month of receipt of the request` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the controller provided the information on action taken without undue delay`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "without undue delay"
        IF `the date the controller provided the information on action taken` AT MOST (`add months` `the date the controller received the request` (`Art 12(3) the months within which the information on action taken is to be provided` `the period has been extended by two further months`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "in any event within one month of receipt of the request"
        -- a month is counted with `add months` from the date of receipt and ends on the same day of the month (clamped to the end of a short month); the other reading, 30 days, is listed under "Marginal readings".

-- src:150 | That period may be extended by two further months where necessary, taking into account the complexity and number of the requests.
@ref Art 12(3) second sentence (src:150)
GIVEN `the extension is necessary, taking into account the complexity and number of the requests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(3) the period may be extended by two further months` MEANS
    IF `the extension is necessary, taking into account the complexity and number of the requests`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); a grant gated by "where", so split site (ii), fork F12-3; the other reading is NOTHING): "where necessary, taking into account the complexity and number of the requests"

-- src:150 | The controller shall inform the data subject of any such extension within one month of receipt of the request, together with the reasons for the delay.
@ref Art 12(3) third sentence (src:150)
GIVEN `the period has been extended by two further months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the controller received the request` IS A DATE
      `the date the controller informed the data subject of the extension` IS A DATE
      `the controller gave the reasons for the delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 12(3) the controller informs the data subject of the extension within one month of receipt of the request, together with the reasons for the delay` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the period has been extended by two further months`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of any such extension": a case with no extension is outside the sentence, and it has no gate word (ruling (c))
        IF `the date the controller informed the data subject of the extension` AT MOST (`add months` `the date the controller received the request` `Art 12(3) the months within which the data subject is to be informed of the extension`) AND `the controller gave the reasons for the delay`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "within one month of receipt of the request, together with the reasons for the delay"

GIVEN `the period has been extended by two further months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 12 action`
`Art 12(3) the controller must provide the data subject with information on action taken on the request` MEANS
    PARTY controller
    MUST `Art 12(3) provide the data subject with information on action taken on the request`
    WITHIN (`Art 12(3) the months within which the information on action taken is to be provided` `the period has been extended by two further months`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY controller BECAUSE "the information on action taken was not provided within one month of receipt of the request (three months where the period was extended)"
    -- the clock counts months from receipt of the request

GIVEN `the period has been extended by two further months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 12 action`
`Art 12(3) the controller must inform the data subject of the extension within one month of receipt of the request` MEANS
    IF `the period has been extended by two further months`
    THEN PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 12(3) inform the data subject of the extension, with the reasons for the delay`
         WITHIN 1
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY controller BECAUSE "the data subject was not informed of the extension within one month of receipt of the request"
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- the clock counts months from receipt of the request; with no extension there is nothing to inform of

-- src:150 | Where the data subject makes the request by electronic form means, the information shall be provided by electronic means where possible, unless otherwise requested by the data subject.
@ref Art 12(3) fourth sentence (src:150)
GIVEN `the data subject makes the request by electronic form means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is possible to provide the information by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject has requested otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is provided by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 12(3) the information is provided by electronic means where the request is made by electronic form means` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the data subject makes the request by electronic form means`)
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "Where", periods ruling (b)): "Where the data subject makes the request by electronic form means"
        IF NOT (`it is possible to provide the information by electronic means`)
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b)): "by electronic means where possible"
        IF `the data subject has requested otherwise`
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "unless"): "unless otherwise requested by the data subject"
        IF `the information is provided by electronic means`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "the information shall be provided by electronic means"

§ `Article 12(4): the reasons for not taking action`

-- src:151 | 4. If the controller does not take action on the request of the data subject, the controller shall inform the data subject without delay and at the latest within one month of receipt of the request of the reasons for not taking action and on the possibility of lodging a complaint with a supervisory authority and seeking a judicial remedy.
@ref Art 12(4): the months allowed for the reasons (src:151)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Art 12(4) the months within which the data subject is to be informed of the reasons for not taking action` MEANS
    1
-- "without delay and at the latest within one month of receipt of the request": no extension is given for the reasons.

-- src:151 | 4. If the controller does not take action on the request of the data subject, the controller shall inform the data subject without delay and at the latest within one month of receipt of the request of the reasons for not taking action and on the possibility of lodging a complaint with a supervisory authority and seeking a judicial remedy.
@ref Art 12(4) (src:151)
GIVEN `the controller does not take action on the request of the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the controller received the request` IS A DATE
      `the date the controller informed the data subject` IS A DATE
      `the controller informed the data subject without delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information includes the reasons for not taking action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information includes the possibility of lodging a complaint with a supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information includes the possibility of seeking a judicial remedy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 12(4) the controller informs the data subject of the reasons for not taking action and of the possibilities of a complaint and a judicial remedy` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the controller does not take action on the request of the data subject`)
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "If", the text says no in its own words): "If the controller does not take action on the request of the data subject"
        IF `the controller informed the data subject without delay`
           AND `the date the controller informed the data subject` AT MOST (`add months` `the date the controller received the request` `Art 12(4) the months within which the data subject is to be informed of the reasons for not taking action`)
           AND `the information includes the reasons for not taking action`
           AND `the information includes the possibility of lodging a complaint with a supervisory authority`
           AND `the information includes the possibility of seeking a judicial remedy`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "shall inform the data subject without delay and at the latest within one month of receipt of the request of the reasons for not taking action and on the possibility of lodging a complaint with a supervisory authority and seeking a judicial remedy"

GIVEN `the controller does not take action on the request of the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 12 action`
`Art 12(4) the controller must inform the data subject of the reasons for not taking action within one month of receipt of the request` MEANS
    IF `the controller does not take action on the request of the data subject`
    THEN PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 12(4) inform the data subject of the reasons for not taking action and of the possibilities of a complaint and a judicial remedy`
         WITHIN 1
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY controller BECAUSE "the data subject was not informed of the reasons for not taking action within one month of receipt of the request"
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- the clock counts months from receipt of the request

§ `Article 12(5): free of charge, the fee, the refusal, the burden`

-- src:152 | Information provided under Articles 13 and 14 and any communication and any actions taken under Articles 15 to 22 and 34 shall be provided free of charge.
@ref Art 12(5) first sentence (src:152)
GIVEN `a fee is charged for the information, communication or action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(5) the information, communication or action is provided free of charge` MEANS
    IF `a fee is charged for the information, communication or action`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i); the exception of points (a) and (b) is asked by `Art 12(5)(a) ...`): "shall be provided free of charge"

-- src:152 | 5. Information provided under Articles 13 and 14 and any communication and any actions taken under Articles 15 to 22 and 34 shall be provided free of charge. Where requests from a data subject are manifestly unfounded or excessive, in particular because of their repetitive character, the controller may either:
-- src:153 | (a) charge a reasonable fee taking into account the administrative costs of providing the information or communication or taking the action requested; or
@ref Art 12(5) second sentence and point (a): a reasonable fee (src:152-153)
GIVEN `the request is manifestly unfounded or excessive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller has demonstrated the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee is reasonable, taking into account the administrative costs of providing the information or communication or taking the action requested` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(5)(a) the controller may charge a reasonable fee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the request is manifestly unfounded or excessive`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "Where", periods ruling (b); a grant gated by "where", split site (ii), fork F12-4): "Where requests from a data subject are manifestly unfounded or excessive, in particular because of their repetitive character, the controller may either"
        IF NOT (`the controller has demonstrated the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (ii), fork F12-5): "The controller shall bear the burden of demonstrating the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request"
        IF `the fee is reasonable, taking into account the administrative costs of providing the information or communication or taking the action requested`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a reasonable fee taking into account the administrative costs of providing the information or communication or taking the action requested": a fee outside that limit is outside the grant, and the text does not say no to it in its own words
    -- "in particular because of their repetitive character": a repetitive request is one way to be manifestly unfounded or excessive, not a second test; it is not read.

-- src:152 | 5. Information provided under Articles 13 and 14 and any communication and any actions taken under Articles 15 to 22 and 34 shall be provided free of charge. Where requests from a data subject are manifestly unfounded or excessive, in particular because of their repetitive character, the controller may either:
-- src:154 | (b) refuse to act on the request.
@ref Art 12(5) second sentence and point (b): refusing to act (src:152-154)
GIVEN `the request is manifestly unfounded or excessive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller has demonstrated the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(5)(b) the controller may refuse to act on the request` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the request is manifestly unfounded or excessive`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "Where", periods ruling (b); a grant gated by "where", split site (ii), fork F12-4): "Where requests from a data subject are manifestly unfounded or excessive, in particular because of their repetitive character, the controller may either"
        IF NOT (`the controller has demonstrated the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (ii), fork F12-5): "The controller shall bear the burden of demonstrating the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:155 | The controller shall bear the burden of demonstrating the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request.
@ref Art 12(5) last sentence: the burden (src:155)
GIVEN `the controller has demonstrated the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(5) the controller has borne the burden of demonstrating the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request` MEANS
    IF `the controller has demonstrated the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i), fork F12-5): "The controller shall bear the burden of demonstrating the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request"

§ `Article 12(6): additional information to confirm identity`

-- src:156 | 6. Without prejudice to Article 11, where the controller has reasonable doubts concerning the identity of the natural person making the request referred to in Articles 15 to 21, the controller may request the provision of additional information necessary to confirm the identity of the data subject.
@ref Art 12(6) (src:156)
GIVEN `the controller has reasonable doubts concerning the identity of the natural person making the request referred to in Articles 15 to 21` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the additional information is necessary to confirm the identity of the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(6) the controller may request the provision of additional information necessary to confirm the identity of the data subject` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the controller has reasonable doubts concerning the identity of the natural person making the request referred to in Articles 15 to 21`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); a grant gated by "where", split site (ii), fork F12-6): "where the controller has reasonable doubts concerning the identity of the natural person making the request referred to in Articles 15 to 21, the controller may request the provision of additional information necessary to confirm the identity of the data subject"
        IF `the additional information is necessary to confirm the identity of the data subject`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "additional information necessary to confirm the identity of the data subject": information that is not necessary for that is outside the grant
    -- "Without prejudice to Article 11": Article 11 continues to apply alongside this paragraph; nothing here reads it.

§ `Article 12(7): standardised icons`

-- src:157 | The information to be provided to data subjects pursuant to Articles 13 and 14 may be provided in combination with standardised icons in order to give in an easily visible, intelligible and clearly legible manner a meaningful overview of the intended processing.
@ref Art 12(7) first sentence (src:157)
GIVEN `the information is to be provided pursuant to Article 13 or Article 14` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(7) the information may be provided in combination with standardised icons` MEANS
    IF `the information is to be provided pursuant to Article 13 or Article 14`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The information to be provided to data subjects pursuant to Articles 13 and 14 may be provided in combination with standardised icons": information under another Article is outside the grant, and the text does not say no to it
    -- "in order to give in an easily visible, intelligible and clearly legible manner a meaningful overview of the intended processing": a purpose clause; it is not read.

-- src:157 | Where the icons are presented electronically they shall be machine-readable.
@ref Art 12(7) second sentence (src:157)
GIVEN `the icons are presented electronically` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the icons are machine-readable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 12(7) the icons presented electronically are machine-readable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the icons are presented electronically`)
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "Where", periods ruling (b)): "Where the icons are presented electronically they shall be machine-readable"
        IF `the icons are machine-readable`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "they shall be machine-readable"
